<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <IsPackable>false</IsPackable>
    <EnforceCodeStyleInBuild>true</EnforceCodeStyleInBuild>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!-- D5 — THE FENCE. IOscSender and UdpOscSender are internal to this assembly, and this list is the
       complete set of assemblies that may see them. MagicChatbox.Vrc owns the safety gates; nothing
       else may reach the wire.

       Adding an entry here re-opens the hole audit F-143 closed in v2 and that ModuleRuntime.cs:604
       still has open. Do not add one. If something needs to send, give it a method on IVrcEgress.

       Exactly ONE production assembly may appear here, and it is MagicChatbox.Vrc. Test assemblies are
       a different case: they substitute the sender to prove the gates cannot be skipped, and they ship
       to nobody. The architecture test asserts this list contains Vrc plus *.Tests and nothing else, so
       a production addition fails the build rather than review. -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="MagicChatbox.Vrc" />
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="MagicChatbox.Osc.Tests" />
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="MagicChatbox.Vrc.Tests" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <!-- This assembly has NO PROJECT REFERENCES, and it stays that way so that "who can reach the wire"
       is answerable by reading one csproj.

       The one package reference is MeaMod.DNS, the mDNS stack. It is here rather than behind a seam in
       another assembly because OSCQuery *is* protocol: advertising _oscjson._tcp and resolving SRV
       records is how the OSC port is negotiated at all (§12.3). MeaMod.DNS ships lib/net7.0, which
       net10.0 consumes without a compatibility shim, and it is the same build VRCOSC and v2 both run in
       production. Discovery still sits behind IOscQueryDiscovery so the rest of the subsystem is
       testable without a multicast socket. -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="MeaMod.DNS" Version="1.0.71" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
